# What Vercel must not upload.
#
# Every `.ts` file under `api/` becomes a Vercel Function — the directory is the
# routing table, not a source folder. Without this file the deployment carried
# four functions instead of one: the entry, both test files and the Vitest
# config, each reachable at its own public path (`/api/health.test` and so on).
#
# They failed on invocation, because `vitest` is not a production dependency, so
# nothing leaked. That is luck rather than design: `deployed-entry.test.ts`
# spawns a compiler, and no test file should be one request away from the
# internet. The function budget is recorded as 1 of 12 in
# .claude/context/backend.md, and `api/one-function.test.ts` fails if a new file
# here is neither the entry nor ignored.
api/*.test.ts
api/vitest.config.ts
